1760	Chapter~\ref{chap:Algebra} along a finite morphism to the projective line yields the
1761	finiteness of \(H^1\). Classically this computation goes back to the explicit \v{C}ech
1762	computation of the cohomology of projective space --- for \(\PP^1\) itself, the
1763	description of \(H^1\) as the cokernel of the two-chart restriction-difference map into
1764	the Laurent ring, spanned by the finitely many ``negative'' monomials --- extended to a
1765	curve by pushing forward along a finite morphism; the two-lattice ladder is exactly the
1766	abstraction of that monomial bookkeeping.
1767	Hartshorne's cited calculation is for projective space over a Noetherian base; it is the
1768	model for the explicit two-chart argument below, whose hypotheses are stated independently.
